WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.233
(playful music)

00:00:01.233 --> 00:00:03.456
- Most people don't think too
much about changing the world,

00:00:03.456 --> 00:00:05.259
but here, we do.

00:00:05.259 --> 00:00:06.176
Right, Joey?

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:16.037
Here at SynDaver Labs in Tampa,
Florida, we make the world's

00:00:16.037 --> 00:00:19.317
most sophisticated synthetic
human tissues and body parts.

00:00:19.317 --> 00:00:21.491
(playful music)

00:00:21.491 --> 00:00:23.233
Just take a look at Joey here.

00:00:23.233 --> 00:00:24.176
While he might look like a real boy,

00:00:24.176 --> 00:00:26.139
he's actually a synthetic cadaver.

00:00:26.139 --> 00:00:29.844
He's made to breathe, bleed
and act just like a real human.

00:00:29.844 --> 00:00:31.945
Joey leads an incredibly interesting life.

00:00:31.945 --> 00:00:33.195
High-five, Joey.

00:00:34.857 --> 00:00:36.873
All this technology he and
and his friends are made of

00:00:36.873 --> 00:00:39.220
allow them to replace
cadavers, live animals

00:00:39.220 --> 00:00:41.220
and even human patients.

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:46.137
A synthetic human takes
about three weeks to build

00:00:46.137 --> 00:00:47.705
from start to finish.

00:00:47.705 --> 00:00:49.348
They're very difficult to build,

00:00:49.348 --> 00:00:50.980
there are thousands of parts.

00:00:50.980 --> 00:00:54.009
If you just look at the
job of assembling one,

00:00:54.009 --> 00:00:56.292
it's staggeringly difficult.

00:00:56.292 --> 00:00:59.097
It takes six specially
trained teams to make Joey.

00:00:59.097 --> 00:01:00.036
Skeletal,

00:01:00.036 --> 00:01:00.975
skin,

00:01:00.975 --> 00:01:02.031
muscles,

00:01:02.031 --> 00:01:03.140
organs,

00:01:03.140 --> 00:01:04.036
vasculature,

00:01:04.036 --> 00:01:05.103
and final assembly.

00:01:05.103 --> 00:01:07.151
And then there's our
tech crew, engineering,

00:01:07.151 --> 00:01:09.284
electronics and tooling.

00:01:09.284 --> 00:01:12.571
Everything that we make
has to be stored in water

00:01:12.571 --> 00:01:14.576
when it's not being used
because it's made, you know,

00:01:14.576 --> 00:01:17.904
primarily of water just
like a every living thing.

00:01:17.904 --> 00:01:20.667
You know, there's always a
high demand for real cadavers.

00:01:20.667 --> 00:01:21.780
The supply is limited.

00:01:21.780 --> 00:01:23.380
They're getting tougher
and tougher to get.

00:01:23.380 --> 00:01:25.439
And with our synthetic cadavers,

00:01:25.439 --> 00:01:28.568
what we're really mimicking is
live tissue not dead tissue,

00:01:28.568 --> 00:01:31.033
so the experience you get
is more like the experience

00:01:31.033 --> 00:01:34.948
you would get with a live
body than a dead body.

00:01:34.948 --> 00:01:37.156
SynDaver technology is
definitely improving the way

00:01:37.156 --> 00:01:40.111
people study medicine,
study medical procedures,

00:01:40.111 --> 00:01:42.000
study medical device development

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:43.675
because it makes the whole system better.

00:01:43.675 --> 00:01:46.501
It allows surgeons to train in procedures

00:01:46.501 --> 00:01:48.624
that they would not be able to train in

00:01:48.624 --> 00:01:51.045
without risking a patient.

00:01:51.045 --> 00:01:52.592
While we'll never know
how Joey spends his time

00:01:52.592 --> 00:01:54.537
after we go home and turn the lights off.

00:01:54.537 --> 00:01:56.841
We do know that once he
moves into his forever home,

00:01:56.841 --> 00:01:59.092
he'll be training people to save lives.

00:01:59.092 --> 00:02:00.425
Atta boy, Joey!

